  "fanTake": "Well, that was about as fun as a high ankle sprain—which, coincidentally, is exactly what we're dealing with now that A.J. Brown is headed to IR for at least four games. We couldn't get out of our own way against Seattle, turning the ball over three times while generating almost nothing offensively (negative EPA per play will do that), and somehow Rhamondre Stevenson managed to be our most impactful player while still posting a negative win probability added. The defense wasn't exactly lights out either, giving up an EPA per play of 0.07. This loss stings, but the injury to Brown might sting worse."
